    <string name="setup_guide_title">Connect your spreadsheet</string>
    <string name="setup_guide_intro">Set up a spreadsheet in your Google Drive, create your private script connection, then paste the deployed web app URL into Settings. Your secret stays stored securely on this phone and is never shown on this guide.</string>
    <string name="setup_step_one">1. Download and upload your spreadsheet template</string>
    <string name="setup_step_one_detail">Download the .xlsx template below, upload it to Google Drive, and convert it to a Google Sheets file (open it with Google Sheets, then choose File → Save as Google Sheets). Category, Priority, and Status cells have selectable lists and color-coded values. Copy the full spreadsheet URL from your browser and paste it here. The app extracts the spreadsheet ID automatically.</string>
    <string name="spreadsheet_url_hint">Google spreadsheet URL</string>
    <string name="download_template">Download .xlsx template</string>
    <string name="invalid_spreadsheet_url">Enter a Google Sheets URL containing /spreadsheets/d/…</string>
    <string name="template_downloaded">Template saved. Upload the .xlsx file to Google Drive and open it as a Google spreadsheet.</string>
    <string name="template_download_failed">Could not save the template: %1$s</string>
    <string name="setup_step_two">2. Generate your private API secret</string>
    <string name="setup_step_two_detail">Tap Generate secret. The app creates a strong random key and stores it securely on this phone. It is not displayed on this guide. When you tap Copy Code.gs, the same saved key is inserted into the script automatically.</string>
    <string name="generate_secret">Generate secret</string>
    <string name="secret_generated">A new secret was generated and saved securely. Tap Copy Code.gs to insert the matching key into your script.</string>
    <string name="secret_already_generated">A secret is already saved securely. It was not changed; the same key will be used in Code.gs.</string>
    <string name="generate_secret_first">Generate a secret before copying Code.gs. The app inserts it into the script without displaying it here.</string>
    <string name="setup_step_three">3. Add the provided Code.gs script</string>
    <string name="setup_step_three_detail">After pasting the spreadsheet URL above and generating your secret, tap Build and copy Code.gs. The app automatically inserts the spreadsheet ID and saved secret into the copied script without displaying the secret. Open the spreadsheet, choose Extensions → Apps Script, replace the editor contents with the copied script, and Save. Select setupWorkbook in the function list and Run it once; approve access when Google asks.</string>
    <string name="view_code">View Code.gs</string>
    <string name="hide_code">Hide Code.gs</string>
    <string name="build_and_copy_code">Build and copy Code.gs</string>
    <string name="code_copied">Code.gs copied. Paste it into the Apps Script editor.</string>
    <string name="ready_code_copied">Your configured Code.gs is copied. Paste it into Extensions → Apps Script. The secret is not displayed on this screen.</string>
    <string name="setup_step_four">4. Deploy as a web app</string>
    <string name="setup_step_four_detail">In Apps Script, tap Deploy → New deployment → select Web app. Set Execute as to Me and Who has access to Anyone, then Deploy and approve Google’s permissions. Copy the Web app URL ending in /exec. After changing the script later, deploy a new version.</string>
    <string name="setup_step_five">5. Finish connecting this app</string>
    <string name="setup_step_five_detail">Open connection settings and paste the deployed /exec URL. The secret generated in this app is already saved securely in the secret field; do not generate a different one. Tap Save and Test connection. A successful test means you are ready to record and report activities.</string>
